@startuml overview
!include ../shared/style.puml
title sd Stage1CustomerService\nScenario map: customer 3 orders Pasta
caption Read the three referenced interactions in order; each is exported separately.
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
actor Manager as M
participant "console : RestaurantRush\n<<boundary>>" as UI
participant "game : RestaurantGame\n<<control>>" as G

note over UI,G
  The game has completed turns 1-6.
  This scenario is part of the documented victory run:
  four paid customers, $51.00, average satisfaction 80.
end note
ref over M,G : S1 Arrival, seating and order (turns 7-8)
ref over M,G : S2 Preparation and service (turns 8-10)
ref over UI,G : S3 Eating and payment (turns 11-12)
note over UI,G
  Service priority on turn 10 preserves satisfaction 76.
  Delaying service to turn 11 would cost another 8 points
  and postpone the payment from turn 12 to turn 13.
end note
loop turn = 13..18
  UI -> G : startTurn()
  activate G
  G --> UI : return
  deactivate G
  M -> UI : choose Waiter and Chef tasks or Wait
  ref over UI,G : Existing phase-checked task protocol (see S1/S2)
  UI -> G : finishTurn()
  activate G
  G --> UI : return
  deactivate G
end
note right of G : phase = FINISHED after turn 18
UI -> G : victory()
activate G
G -> G : paidCount()\naveragePaidSatisfaction()
alt paid >= 4 and revenue >= 4500 and average >= 60
  G --> UI : true
  UI --> M : display VICTORY and totals
else any target fails
  G --> UI : false
  UI --> M : display DEFEAT and totals
end
deactivate G
footer Ch. 7: ref, loop and alt fragments | Ref names identify the companion sequence diagrams.
@enduml
